  "coverage_note": "Municipal rows are the ministry appraisal for free-market housing in municipalities of more than 25,000 inhabitants. The sheet splits the mean into homes up to five years old and older homes. Up to five years is the comparison used for Avena's new-build asking prices, and it is still an appraisal of that age, not a transaction price. A cell printed n.r. is withheld by the ministry and stays blank. A place the sheet does not name, including a municipality of 25,000 inhabitants or fewer and a district that is not itself the municipality, has no official figure. A neighbouring municipality is not substituted. A median and a gap are published only for a town with at least 8 listings that have a positive asking €/m². The sheet's own province label is kept, including where two Castellón municipalities are printed in the Alicante block.",
  "caveats": [
    "Avena's figure is the median asking price per m² of coastal new-build listings in the current corpus. It is not a price at which a home has sold, and it is not the median of every home in the municipality.",
    "The ministry figure is the mean appraised value per m² of free-market housing. The up-to-five-years column is homes of that age. It is not limited to dwellings sold as new, and it is not a notarial or registered transaction price.",
    "The all-ages column mixes those homes with older ones. A gap against it is labelled all-ages. It is not copied into the up-to-five-years gap when that cell is n.r.",
    "The sheet covers municipalities of more than 25,000 inhabitants. Smaller municipalities, and Avena place names that are districts rather than the municipality, are absent. Their absence is not filled in.",
    "Towns with fewer than 8 listings that have a positive asking €/m² are marked insufficient. No median and no gap is published for them. The ministry figure is still shown when the town matched a row.",
    "No comparison on this page is a statistic published by the ministry, INE, the notaries or the registrars."
  ],
